{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Heart</b>, <b>heart</b>, <b>all</b> — three linked words. [See verse 14–15.]" "<b>It will make glad</b> — from the root טובת מראה, a beautiful appearance of the face." "<b>A broken spirit</b> — and it is broken, therefore it does not learn knowledge. But an understanding heart that rejoices and has no sorrow in the world, it will seek to learn knowledge."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The bracketed cross-reference is already present in the Hebrew source."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:01.805301477Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}